1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:33,737 --> 00:01:37,497
I seem to have gotten addicted to the smoked mutton here.

17
00:01:38,247 --> 00:01:41,497
I also wanted to meet you again to trade information.

18
00:01:41,497 --> 00:01:43,957
I got so drunk last time that I completely forgot.

19
00:01:43,957 --> 00:01:46,507
Now that you mention it, you're right.

20
00:01:46,507 --> 00:01:50,837
I myself got distracted by your wife's entrancing story.

21
00:01:51,957 --> 00:01:53,967
Don't let yourself be entranced by her gossip.

22
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:58,477
Oh, come now. I think your wife's an amazing person.

23
00:01:58,477 --> 00:02:03,477
Wolf and the Helpless Partner

24
00:02:04,097 --> 00:02:06,277
Thanks for a great night.

25
00:02:06,277 --> 00:02:07,147
See you.

26
00:02:07,147 --> 00:02:07,817
You too.

27
00:02:08,937 --> 00:02:12,067
I've seen what this "Zheren" looks like now.

28
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:14,487
I'll continue with the investigation.

29
00:02:14,487 --> 00:02:15,947
Please do.

30
00:02:16,447 --> 00:02:18,577
I was surprised, to be honest.

31
00:02:18,577 --> 00:02:21,407
I never would have expected your story yesterday to be true.

32
00:02:22,577 --> 00:02:27,827
You thought it was simple fraud at first, but then you looked deeper and found something more complex.

33
00:02:27,837 --> 00:02:31,707
For the sake of obtaining massive amounts of depreciating currency,

34
00:02:31,707 --> 00:02:34,377
that man goes around spreading rumors that the coin's value will rise.

35
00:02:34,717 --> 00:02:38,137
This causes several merchants to begin collecting it.

36
00:02:38,597 --> 00:02:43,807
When its value depreciates,
those merchants rush to get rid of it.

37
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:48,237
Then someone makes an appearance and purchases the coins when the time is right.

38
00:02:48,237 --> 00:02:53,777
The merchants who were deceived dare not speak about it in order to preserve their reputation.

39
00:02:54,777 --> 00:03:00,497
And as you said, there is a method that can reap huge profits out of a depreciating currency.

40
00:03:01,617 --> 00:03:05,627
But one that comes at a substantial risk.

41
00:03:06,627 --> 00:03:09,717
My curiosity has been piqued.

42
00:03:10,417 --> 00:03:11,507
I'm happy to hear it.

43
00:03:11,507 --> 00:03:13,587
It's for the sake of future business,

44
00:03:14,297 --> 00:03:16,587
much like the deal for the marten furs.

45
00:03:19,347 --> 00:03:21,347
Do you think we'll be in time?

46
00:03:23,057 --> 00:03:25,557
Even if you're right about Zheren,

47
00:03:25,557 --> 00:03:31,647
our plan to best his employer will be for nothing if Milone Trading doesn't act quickly.

48
00:03:31,647 --> 00:03:34,777
Well, I think things will work out.

49
00:03:36,077 --> 00:03:43,247
A company with enough resources to open foreign branches should be able to track a single person.

50
00:03:46,607 --> 00:03:47,327
What's so funny?

51
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:49,867
It's just...

52
00:03:51,467 --> 00:03:53,707
I was just reminiscing.

53
00:03:55,297 --> 00:03:56,427
Did I do something?

54
00:03:56,987 --> 00:04:03,097
Well, he'd do the same thing you did, but he'd always fall.

55
00:04:04,057 --> 00:04:07,187
It didn't matter how many times I warned him.

56
00:04:07,187 --> 00:04:09,357
He sounds like a fun person.

57
00:04:09,357 --> 00:04:12,737
Yes. He was a bit foolish, but very cheerful.

58
00:04:13,157 --> 00:04:16,777
He wasn't surprised in the least
when he saw me in my wolf form.

59
00:04:16,777 --> 00:04:19,367
I suppose he was a bit odd,

60
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:20,867
but a good fellow nonetheless.

61
00:04:21,287 --> 00:04:25,247
He was the first person who treated me kindly, without prejudice.

62
00:04:25,247 --> 00:04:27,207
He was from Pasloei.

63
00:04:27,207 --> 00:04:30,167
Are you talking about the one who entrusted you with the wheat fields?

64
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:30,957
Yes.

65
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:34,127
He was so silly.

66
00:04:35,217 --> 00:04:37,087
Sometimes I didn't know what to do with him.

67
00:04:48,377 --> 00:04:49,267
What's the matter?

68
00:04:49,817 --> 00:04:51,767
I wanted to tell you something.

69
00:04:52,647 --> 00:04:55,607
I thought I did, but now it's gone.

70
00:04:55,607 --> 00:04:56,767
Seriously?

71
00:04:57,067 --> 00:04:59,947
I think it was important, but I can't...

72
00:05:00,527 --> 00:05:02,647
In that case, I'm sure you'll remember eventually.

73
00:05:03,857 --> 00:05:05,117
I suppose so.

74
00:05:12,537 --> 00:05:15,077
A friend, huh?

75
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:32,527
I'm Marlheit, the manager of this branch.

76
00:05:32,927 --> 00:05:36,517
We'd like to accept your offer.

77
00:05:36,517 --> 00:05:40,117
Does that mean you've figured out who Zheren is working for?

78
00:05:40,117 --> 00:05:43,897
Yes, he's receiving support from Medio Trading.

79
00:05:44,517 --> 00:05:46,147
Medio Trading?

80
00:05:46,687 --> 00:05:49,787
I see. They're Pazzio's leading agricultural broker,

81
00:05:49,787 --> 00:05:52,137
not to mention the amount of cargo ships they own.

82
00:05:52,917 --> 00:05:58,957
It would be impossible for them to carry out this plan you envision on their own.

83
00:05:58,957 --> 00:06:03,097
We assume there is a nobleman operating behind the scenes,

84
00:06:03,097 --> 00:06:05,717
though we haven't been able to identify him yet.

85
00:06:05,717 --> 00:06:07,787
Nonetheless, as you've pointed out,

86
00:06:07,787 --> 00:06:11,767
it is of little concern to us if we take the initiative.

87
00:06:13,187 --> 00:06:16,437
Let's discuss how to split the profit.

88
00:06:18,607 --> 00:06:21,107
You're more cheerful than I've ever seen you before.

89
00:06:22,407 --> 00:06:24,157
We could round up 300,000...

90
00:06:24,157 --> 00:06:27,407
No, make that 400,000 Trenni silver coins if everything goes well.

91
00:06:27,407 --> 00:06:33,837
If Milone profits ten percent from each Trenni coin,
I'll finally be able to own a store with my share of 2,000!

92
00:06:35,377 --> 00:06:38,207
Well, I'm glad everything's going well.

93
00:06:41,387 --> 00:06:43,967
Didn't I tell you to rest at the inn if you had a hangover?

94
00:06:43,967 --> 00:06:47,347
I was worried that they might get the better of you.

95
00:06:47,807 --> 00:06:49,137
What's that supposed to mean?

96
00:06:49,597 --> 00:06:51,057
I meant exactly what I said.

97
00:06:52,067 --> 00:06:53,357
Geez.

98
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:57,527
Hang in there. We're almost at the inn.

99
00:07:18,447 --> 00:07:20,047
A drawing of a shop?

100
00:07:20,047 --> 00:07:21,967
Don't act so surprised.

101
00:07:21,967 --> 00:07:24,297
When did you wake up?

102
00:07:24,797 --> 00:07:27,347
Your art isn't bad!

103
00:07:27,347 --> 00:07:28,887
You're flattering me.

104
00:07:28,887 --> 00:07:31,887
Are you planning to open a store soon, then?

105
00:07:32,247 --> 00:07:34,977
Only if the project with Milone Trading goes well,

106
00:07:34,977 --> 00:07:37,007
not that I have any doubt it will.

107
00:07:40,387 --> 00:07:44,197
Owning a store is every traveling merchant's dream.

108
00:07:44,737 --> 00:07:46,147
I'm no exception.

109
00:07:46,467 --> 00:07:49,157
You get to be part of a community once you own a store.

110
00:07:49,537 --> 00:07:54,167
On the road, I can't make close friends or have a fair chance of finding a wife.

111
00:07:55,377 --> 00:07:58,167
Speaking of which, I wonder how Chloe's doing.

112
00:07:58,667 --> 00:08:01,337
If she heard I opened a shop, she'd be shocked.

113
00:08:01,337 --> 00:08:03,377
More than that, she'd be peeved.

114
00:08:04,927 --> 00:08:07,677
That could be bad for me, though.

115
00:08:08,887 --> 00:08:09,677
Why's that?

116
00:08:10,137 --> 00:08:14,017
Once you open a store,
you won't want to leave it, right?

117
00:08:14,017 --> 00:08:18,687
I'll have to travel alone or find another companion.

118
00:08:19,177 --> 00:08:23,537
You've got your wits, and you still have the money earned from the marten fur.

119
00:08:23,537 --> 00:08:25,237
You won't have any trouble alone.

120
00:08:27,907 --> 00:08:29,657
I'm tired of being alone.

121
00:08:33,537 --> 00:08:37,827
I don't have the right to force you to come with me.

122
00:08:38,417 --> 00:08:39,667
Right?

123
00:08:41,007 --> 00:08:44,327
I'd still accompany you on your way back home to the north.

124
00:08:50,737 --> 00:08:52,097
Even when the money comes in,

125
00:08:52,097 --> 00:08:54,217
I won't be able to open a store right away.

126
00:08:55,847 --> 00:08:57,397
Truly?

127
00:08:57,397 --> 00:08:59,227
Why would I lie?

128
00:09:04,767 --> 00:09:08,317
So... come on. Don't make that kind of face.

129
00:09:09,907 --> 00:09:10,657
Okay.

130
00:09:57,607 --> 00:09:59,207
This isn't like you.

131
00:10:00,477 --> 00:10:03,167
I keep seeing the same dream.

132
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:04,457
Dream?

133
00:10:04,457 --> 00:10:08,967
When I... When I wake up, nobody is there.

134
00:10:10,077 --> 00:10:14,467
Yue, Inty, Paro and Muri...

135
00:10:14,897 --> 00:10:17,887
No matter where I look, they're nowhere to be found.

136
00:10:19,597 --> 00:10:22,977
We're able to live for hundreds of years.

137
00:10:23,477 --> 00:10:26,947
So... So I thought I would go traveling.

138
00:10:27,657 --> 00:10:31,237
I was sure, so very sure, that I'd see them all again,

139
00:10:31,907 --> 00:10:34,497
but... they were gone. There was no one.

140
00:10:35,647 --> 00:10:38,597
I don't want to open my eyes and find no one there.

141
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,567
I'm tired of being alone.

142
00:10:41,197 --> 00:10:42,537
It's cold when I'm by myself.

143
00:10:43,537 --> 00:10:45,917
It's lonely when I'm by myself.

144
00:10:50,707 --> 00:10:52,177
I lost my composure.

145
00:10:52,177 --> 00:10:54,667
Those kinds of dreams tend to haunt traveling merchants, too.

146
00:10:56,707 --> 00:10:58,887
Your face is a mess.

147
00:10:58,887 --> 00:10:59,977
Hold on.

148
00:11:04,647 --> 00:11:05,647
Here.

149
00:11:05,647 --> 00:11:06,687
But this is your...

150
00:11:07,397 --> 00:11:09,647
I always throw these away when I'm done.

151
00:11:09,647 --> 00:11:12,857
And the deal isn't even finished yet.

152
00:11:13,447 --> 00:11:15,437
I won't count my chickens before they hatch.

153
00:11:23,707 --> 00:11:26,117
I'm in your debt now.

154
00:11:29,547 --> 00:11:32,587
I'm still sleepy. Aren't you going to bed?

155
00:11:32,587 --> 00:11:34,597
I suppose it's about time.

156
00:11:34,597 --> 00:11:35,927
We don't want to waste candles.

157
00:11:38,097 --> 00:11:40,057
Spoken like a true merchant.

158
00:12:01,077 --> 00:12:01,997
W-What—

159
00:12:01,997 --> 00:12:04,377
Don't be a boor.

160
00:12:10,827 --> 00:12:12,257
Can't... breathe...

161
00:12:17,677 --> 00:12:19,627
Have your eyes become used to the dark?

162
00:12:21,977 --> 00:12:23,137
What do you—

163
00:12:23,637 --> 00:12:27,607
I finally remembered what was so important.

164
00:12:28,837 --> 00:12:30,897
There are three men outside the door.

165
00:12:30,897 --> 00:12:33,317
I don't think they're guests of the inn.

166
00:12:33,687 --> 00:12:35,607
Don't tell me they're from Medio Trading.

167
00:12:37,407 --> 00:12:38,987
We're on the second floor.

168
00:12:38,987 --> 00:12:41,027
Fortunately for us, there's no one outside.

169
00:12:41,437 --> 00:12:43,237
Are you ready?

170
00:12:45,077 --> 00:12:49,837
Come, see my body underneath the moonlight!

171
00:13:01,417 --> 00:13:02,637
Run for it.

172
00:13:03,057 --> 00:13:04,887
You'll have to give up the wagon.

173
00:13:12,937 --> 00:13:15,647
They have no reason to kill the horse.

174
00:13:15,647 --> 00:13:17,187
We can get it back later.

175
00:13:17,567 --> 00:13:18,317
Yeah.

176
00:13:26,917 --> 00:13:30,417
Hold on to some of this just in case.

177
00:13:33,377 --> 00:13:34,127
It's warm.

178
00:13:34,127 --> 00:13:36,167
It's the wheat in which I live.

179
00:13:36,627 --> 00:13:38,467
They're heading for Milone Trading!

180
00:13:39,967 --> 00:13:42,127
Keep them from getting inside at all costs!

181
00:13:44,927 --> 00:13:48,477
Holo, let's go shopping when this is all over.

182
00:13:48,477 --> 00:13:50,267
What are you saying at a time like this?

183
00:13:50,267 --> 00:13:52,517
I'll buy you a comb or a hat.

184
00:13:52,517 --> 00:13:54,067
What are you up to now?

185
00:13:54,067 --> 00:13:57,027
It's just that I noticed how beautiful your hair is.

186
00:14:00,587 --> 00:14:02,737
I'd prefer a comb for my tail rather than my hair.

187
00:14:03,077 --> 00:14:04,487
That's fine with me.

188
00:14:04,997 --> 00:14:06,987
Hang in there. We're almost at Milone Trading.

189
00:14:10,377 --> 00:14:11,207
Did you see them?

190
00:14:11,207 --> 00:14:12,247
No.

191
00:14:12,247 --> 00:14:13,747
They're bound to be nearby.

192
00:14:13,747 --> 00:14:16,467
It's only a matter of time before backup comes. Surround them!

193
00:14:16,467 --> 00:14:17,257
Yes, sir!

194
00:14:20,467 --> 00:14:22,717
It seems like we're in trouble.

195
00:14:22,717 --> 00:14:24,427
Should we split up?

196
00:14:24,427 --> 00:14:27,227
A nice idea, but I have a better plan.

197
00:14:27,227 --> 00:14:27,887
What is it?

198
00:14:28,387 --> 00:14:31,267
I'll run toward the main street and draw them off.

199
00:14:31,267 --> 00:14:32,267
Then you'll be able to—

200
00:14:32,267 --> 00:14:33,937
Wait a second! I can't let you—

201
00:14:33,937 --> 00:14:34,977
Listen.

202
00:14:34,977 --> 00:14:38,947
If we split up, you're the one who'll get caught.

203
00:14:38,947 --> 00:14:41,357
I'm a wolf. I'd evade them.

204
00:14:41,817 --> 00:14:45,667
If I escape by myself, how am I supposed to get Milone to help?

205
00:14:46,617 --> 00:14:49,287
You've already told Milone everything.

206
00:14:49,287 --> 00:14:54,167
The only influence we have over them is the threat of your betrayal.

207
00:14:56,207 --> 00:14:57,797
No, I can't do it.

208
00:14:57,797 --> 00:15:02,797
If Medio Trading sees your ears and tail,
they'll bring you to the Church for sure.

209
00:15:02,797 --> 00:15:04,427
They can't catch me.

210
00:15:04,427 --> 00:15:08,597
Even if they get ahold of me, I'll just keep my ears and tail hidden for a day.

211
00:15:08,597 --> 00:15:11,597
I know you'll save me by then.

212
00:15:12,057 --> 00:15:12,937
Come on.

213
00:15:12,937 --> 00:15:15,927
Your dream is to own a shop, is it not?

214
00:15:16,527 --> 00:15:20,437
And just a minute ago, I told you that I was in your debt.

215
00:15:20,447 --> 00:15:22,157
Don't be ridiculous!

216
00:15:22,157 --> 00:15:23,987
If you're caught, you'll be killed!

217
00:15:23,987 --> 00:15:26,187
That's not repayment. It's suicide!

218
00:15:27,287 --> 00:15:29,247
Solitude is a fatal disease.

219
00:15:29,957 --> 00:15:31,407
It's a fair trade.

220
00:15:32,787 --> 00:15:33,197
No—

221
00:15:38,867 --> 00:15:40,377
I believe in you.

222
00:15:44,967 --> 00:15:45,797
That way!

223
00:15:45,797 --> 00:15:46,967
We found them!

224
00:15:46,967 --> 00:15:48,637
Roita Street!

225
00:15:48,637 --> 00:15:49,677
Where?

226
00:15:50,517 --> 00:15:51,847
I only see one!

227
00:15:51,847 --> 00:15:53,597
There should be two of them!

228
00:15:54,807 --> 00:15:55,857
There he is!

229
00:16:06,087 --> 00:16:09,327
I'm Lawrence, from this afternoon!
I'm being chased! Help me!

230
00:16:09,327 --> 00:16:10,497
Help me!

231
00:16:10,497 --> 00:16:11,907
There he is!

232
00:16:20,367 --> 00:16:23,797
Wait, you! Give that man to us!

233
00:16:25,677 --> 00:16:26,877
Vermin!

234
00:16:27,547 --> 00:16:32,727
This is the Milone Trading building, owned by Marquis Milone, recognized by His Grace,

235
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:35,637
the thirty-third Archduke Raondeal!

236
00:16:35,637 --> 00:16:38,567
This gate is the property of the Marquis.

237
00:16:38,567 --> 00:16:41,107
Anyone within these walls is his guest!

238
00:16:41,107 --> 00:16:45,727
Furthermore, any guest of the Marquis is under the protection of Archduke Raondeal.

239
00:16:45,727 --> 00:16:47,027
Know this!

240
00:16:47,027 --> 00:16:49,737
When you strike this gate with your cudgels,

241
00:16:49,737 --> 00:16:52,447
you strike the foot of His Grace's throne!

242
00:16:56,327 --> 00:16:57,787
Retreat for now!

243
00:16:59,877 --> 00:17:02,167
That's quite a commotion so late at night.

244
00:17:02,727 --> 00:17:04,287
What's going on here?

245
00:17:06,397 --> 00:17:08,177
I apologize for the disturbance.

246
00:17:08,177 --> 00:17:10,627
I offer my deepest gratitude for your sanctuary.

247
00:17:11,177 --> 00:17:14,767
Save your gratitude for Marquis Milone, though he's not here to hear it.

248
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:17,307
What did they want?

249
00:17:17,307 --> 00:17:20,727
They're undoubtedly lackeys from Medio Trading.

250
00:17:21,397 --> 00:17:22,517
That was my thought.

251
00:17:22,857 --> 00:17:27,157
They caught wind of my business with you, so they were sent to prevent it from—

252
00:17:27,157 --> 00:17:28,517
Prevent it?

253
00:17:28,987 --> 00:17:31,607
I believe that my companion was captured.

254
00:17:31,607 --> 00:17:34,367
Can you help me rescue her?

255
00:17:36,367 --> 00:17:40,737
After the commotion here, I sent some of my men to follow them.

256
00:17:40,737 --> 00:17:46,007
They reported seeing a young lady being taken, apparently against her will.

257
00:17:47,257 --> 00:17:50,507
That must have been my companion, Holo.

258
00:17:50,507 --> 00:17:53,087
She chose to act as a decoy so that I could make it here.

259
00:17:54,347 --> 00:17:55,847
I see.

260
00:17:56,267 --> 00:17:59,767
But why would they want to capture Miss Holo?

261
00:17:59,767 --> 00:18:00,937
I already—

262
00:18:01,857 --> 00:18:06,597
I expect it's because we joined with your company in trying to obstruct their plans.

263
00:18:08,237 --> 00:18:10,687
Don't you think that's strange?

264
00:18:11,237 --> 00:18:12,277
What's strange?!

265
00:18:13,197 --> 00:18:14,577
Please calm down.

266
00:18:14,577 --> 00:18:18,077
Something is very, very wrong.

267
00:18:18,077 --> 00:18:19,627
What makes you think that?

268
00:18:19,627 --> 00:18:21,787
Let me put it this way.

269
00:18:21,787 --> 00:18:26,667
Is there anything they could prevent by taking you two hostage?

270
00:18:26,667 --> 00:18:30,547
We've already started collecting Trenni silver coins.

271
00:18:30,547 --> 00:18:36,427
In other words, we understand the entirety of this opportunity.

272
00:18:36,427 --> 00:18:39,687
They may have had reason to hold you hostage

273
00:18:39,687 --> 00:18:44,937
if you had instructed us to collect Trenni silver coins without telling us why.

274
00:18:44,927 --> 00:18:49,307
However, no company would have taken action based on such a vague suggestion.

275
00:18:50,157 --> 00:18:52,407
Surely you don't mean...

276
00:18:52,407 --> 00:18:56,817
I do. We already have all the information we need to turn a profit.

277
00:18:56,817 --> 00:19:00,907
The fate of you and your partner changes nothing.

278
00:19:02,517 --> 00:19:07,537
It's a terrible turn of events, but we've already invested a substantial amount of money.

279
00:19:07,917 --> 00:19:14,007
If we had to choose between a lucrative profit and bearing your grudge,

280
00:19:14,757 --> 00:19:18,847
I'm sorry to say that our interests would always come first.

281
00:19:18,847 --> 00:19:19,847
However...

282
00:19:19,847 --> 00:19:21,297
<i>Oh my God.</i>

283
00:19:36,567 --> 00:19:37,817
Hold on!

284
00:19:38,947 --> 00:19:41,317
I can see that your partner is important to you.

285
00:19:41,787 --> 00:19:44,327
Any effort to rescue her will fail

286
00:19:44,327 --> 00:19:46,197
without a calm and collected mindset.

287
00:19:49,467 --> 00:19:50,797
My apologies.

288
00:19:50,797 --> 00:19:51,497
That's okay.

289
00:19:52,177 --> 00:19:57,217
I wouldn't be able to stay calm if my wife were in a similar situation.

290
00:19:58,557 --> 00:20:00,427
Like I said, it's strange.

291
00:20:00,927 --> 00:20:05,597
Medio Trading would know how our company would decide, right?

292
00:20:06,567 --> 00:20:08,597
Of course.

293
00:20:08,937 --> 00:20:16,237
They still went after you in spite of the fact that you would have no value in potential negotiations.

294
00:20:16,237 --> 00:20:19,077
Can you think of why that might be?

295
00:20:19,907 --> 00:20:21,247
A reason why...

296
00:20:22,037 --> 00:20:22,947
Don't tell me...

297
00:20:22,957 --> 00:20:27,157
The profits before us are colossal.

298
00:20:27,497 --> 00:20:29,457
We'd very much like to see this plan succeed.

299
00:20:29,457 --> 00:20:30,087
But...

300
00:20:30,087 --> 00:20:33,807
Don't hesitate to say what's on your mind, no matter how trivial.

301
00:20:34,677 --> 00:20:36,127
Mr. Lawrence!

302
00:20:36,467 --> 00:20:37,967
There is something, right?

303
00:20:37,967 --> 00:20:39,387
You do know something.

304
00:20:45,057 --> 00:20:46,767
Excuse me.

305
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:47,427
What is it?

306
00:20:47,767 --> 00:20:50,427
We just received a letter.

307
00:20:50,427 --> 00:20:52,437
I believe it concerns our current situation.

308
00:20:56,617 --> 00:20:59,737
"To the wolf and the forest in which the wolf resides"?

309
00:21:03,707 --> 00:21:07,117
Excuse me, but may I take a look at the letter first?

310
00:21:10,247 --> 00:21:11,627
Very well.

311
00:21:11,627 --> 00:21:12,577
Thank you.

312
00:21:20,017 --> 00:21:21,847
"We have the wolf."

313
00:21:21,847 --> 00:21:24,637
"The Church welcomes all with open arms."

314
00:21:24,637 --> 00:21:26,597
"To keep the wolf away from your home,

315
00:21:26,597 --> 00:21:28,977
keep the door shut and secure your family inside."

316
00:21:35,987 --> 00:21:38,067
Holo, the girl I was traveling with,

317
00:21:40,117 --> 00:21:43,107
is a wolf that controls harvests in human form.

318
00:22:07,347 --> 00:22:08,397
You're...

319
00:23:40,807 --> 00:23:43,927
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Lovers' Quarrel".</i>

320
00:23:45,897 --> 00:23:48,687
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Lovers' Quarrel".</i>

